    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file 'similarity_score.py' that computes cosine similarity between two embedded texts using an external provider, I will use the Hugging Face Transformers library, which is a concrete external provider for natural language processing tasks. The specific model I will use is 'sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2', which is a model for generating embeddings. The code will import the necessary components from the Hugging Face library and use the model to generate embeddings for the input texts. Then, it will compute the cosine similarity between the embeddings. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862791644,
          "start": 1789862787383
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc22b937001eDmRFU5GxTc9bC",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc22b50200165ULEd5xRK3KRh",
